<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zaccaria</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Zaccaria family</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Zaccaria were a Genoese merchant family who built an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aegean">Aegean</a> domain in the late 13th and 14th centuries. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benedetto-zaccaria">Benedetto Zaccaria</a> received the alum mines of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phocaea">Phocaea</a> from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantines</a> and occupied Chios in 1304, which the family held until 1329. A later branch, through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/centurione-ii-zaccaria">Centurione II Zaccaria</a>, ruled the Principality of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaea">Achaea</a> until 1430.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zaccaria.jpg" alt="Zaccaria" width="320" height="374" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ElOsoUgui99 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_arms_of_Zaccaria_(Genoa).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
